"JH" <no@email> writes:
> Just for fun, I added doppelgangers as a playable race (somewhat like
> slashem, slightly different), seeing how simple it was (relatively speaking)
> to add what I think is an interesting choice for a race, so I was toying
> with the idea of creating Lizardmen as a playable race.  Basically, they
> would be humans with a bit lower charisma (no one likes to talk to large
> lizards :)) who start with the ability to swim.  The thing I'm not quite
> sure about is how should they swim?  Magical breathing or water walking
> could be a starting intrinsic, but I'm not sure which would be more
> appropriate.

Why not just give them the swimming intrinsic? Add M1_SWIM to the
lizardman monster definition and use the same fix-up in role_init() as
currently for infravision. (You could make them amphibious as well,
but that would probably be overpowered; making them unbreathing on top
of _that_ would definitely be so.)

And I agree with Boudewijn that you probably want to give them
slightly more defining characteristics than those; playing with the
racial enadv and hpadv factors is probably the easiest way to directly
affect balance.

